  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Major release — every execution tool now returns structured JSON instead of plain strings, plus new tools for compile-once-apply-many, parameter binding, secondary documents, spec-aware streamability analysis, and MCP discoverability. AI agents can now parse failures and self-correct using source-location-aware errors. Highlights: xslt_compile + xslt_apply with SHA256 handle cache; stylesheet parameter binding via JSON; secondary-document registration for doc()/document() against in-memory XML; xslt_explain_streamability with per-mode and per-template streamability analysis (catches the streaming mistakes models make most often); xslt_find_examples with 8 curated working examples (xsl:merge, xsl:fork, xsl:accumulator, xsl:iterate, streaming-mode, xsl:package, fn:transform, xsl:evaluate); xslt_suggest_fix with top-10 error-code rules; xslt_compare_versions; xslt_test assertion runner; server_capabilities; 4 MCP prompts for guided workflows; browsable spec corpus via xslt:// resources. Runtime exception handling narrowed to engine-specific types — no more silently swallowed OOM/cancellation. Structured error codes XMCP0001 (unknown handle), XMCP0002 (bad parameters JSON), XMCP0003 (bad documents JSON). Fixed: invalid XPath in xpath_evaluate previously leaked XQueryParseException; relative URIs in doc() now work in xslt_apply. See RELEASES.md for the full per-phase changelog.",
